  "body": "### Summary\nTwo app-hosted tests assume a regular iPhone size and fail when the whole `SwiftHFRTests` target runs on the iPhone Duo simulator (cover screen 466 × 678 pt, right safe area 84 pt). CI runs on an iPhone 18 Pro, so CI never sees it. Found by mac/M1 while checking #681.\n\n### Facts (iPhone Duo simulator, iPhone19,4, iOS 27.2, folded; `dev-swift` 1df2121a + #1083's tests only)\n- `ComposerLayoutHostedTests.theCardAndTheFloatingButtonsAreTheSharedGapFromTheEdges()` fails on `402 - card.maxX - gap`: the test hard-codes a 402 pt width.\n- `ReaderUnderBarsTests.inANavigationStackTheTopBarAndTheBottomBarReachThePage()` fails on `insets.bottom >= 44`.\n- Not yet run on a non-Duo simulator in the same session to confirm they pass there; CI passes them on the iPhone 18 Pro.\n\n### Scope\n- Make both tests derive their expectations from the window they run in (width, safe area), not from a fixed iPhone size; or state and assert the device they need.\n- Check whether either one hides a real layout issue on the Duo cover screen (the composer card's gap at the right safe area; the bottom bar inset).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Both tests pass on the iPhone 18 Pro and on the iPhone Duo simulator, with expectations taken from the window.\n- [ ] If a real Duo layout gap is found, it gets its own issue.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
